<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_5/e_0074> <http://digistrucmed.org/entityType> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-type/CONDITION_OR_FINDING> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_5/na_0053> <http://digistrucmed.org/deonticForce> "ADVISORY" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_5/tu_0046> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "If urea, creatinine, or $K^+$ does rise excessively, consider stopping concomitant nephrotoxic drugs (e.g. NSAIDsd) and other $K^+$ supplements or retaining agents (triamterene, amiloride) and, if no signs of congestion, reducing the dose of diuretic. This is particularly true in those patients on an SGLT2 inhibitor." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_5/na_0016> <http://digistrucmed.org/deonticForce> "NOT_STATED" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_5/na_0037> <http://digistrucmed.org/operation> "DISCONTINUE" .
